            <h2>Pricing context across companies</h2>
            <p>Advertised prices vary widely across these companies. The most reliable comparison is not sticker price but <em>total installed price</em> at your specific Washington County cemetery, including:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>Stone with all engraving (name, dates, epitaph, symbols, temple silhouette)</li>
              <li>Digital design layout at real scale</li>
              <li>Sexton coordination and cemetery permit / approval</li>
              <li>Required concrete apron / mow strip (Tonaquint, Ivins, Hurricane, and most municipal cemeteries)</li>
              <li>Freight to your specific cemetery</li>
              <li>Professional setting under sexton supervision</li>
              <li>First-year maintenance cleaning</li>
            </ul>
            <p>Ask every provider for an itemized quote showing each of these as separate lines. Prices that look better on the sticker often exclude line items that appear on the invoice at delivery.</p>
            <p>Our public pricing guide is at <a href="/resources/pricing" class="text-bronze font-medium underline hover:text-evergreen transition-colors">/resources/pricing</a>. Direct-to-family pricing typically runs 30–60% less than the same monument bought through a funeral home.</p>
